%% Screen capture (ADR 009 Part 4): an output session's frame on GL, dma-buf and shm.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client (grim, xdpw, wf-recorder)
    participant W as wire_capture (UI)
    participant T as tick_ui (UI)
    participant R as render thread (capture_renderer)
    participant K as worker
    participant P as readiness poller (UI)

    C->>W: create_session(source, options)
    W-->>C: buffer_size, shm_format, dmabuf_device, dmabuf_format, done
    C->>W: create_frame, attach_buffer, damage_buffer, capture
    W->>T: capture_decide (lock, VT pause, power, constraints)
    alt locked
        T->>R: curtain job (glClear / memset)
    else held (VT away, output off)
        T->>T: frame waits
    else
        T->>R: output job {since_seq, client damage, paint_cursors, lock_epoch}
    end
    Note over R: waits for its output to composite something new (no clock started)
    R->>R: composite_output → damage ring record(seq)
    R->>R: lock_epoch moved past the job → cancelled
    alt dma-buf
        R->>R: glBlitFramebuffer per rect into the imported buffer (+ pointer quad), native fence
        R-->>T: completion {fence} (channel; one UI task posted)
        T->>P: fence fd
        P-->>W: signalled
    else shm
        R->>R: blit into the session's LINEAR GBM buffer, native fence; session busy
        R->>K: worker_read
        K->>K: wait fence, gbm_bo_map, copy damaged rows into the shm under its guard (+ pointer blend)
        K-->>T: completion {ready} (channel; UI task posted)
    end
    T->>W: capture_complete: completion from an older lock epoch → decided again
    W-->>C: transform, damage, presentation_time, ready
